["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"A question is defined by the act of seeking information, not the question mark A real question is defined by its function, not its form; asking is a power you can practise — and most of the answers AI hands out today have not answered any question that was seriously posed. Philosophy Bites Philosophy Bites Lani Watson on the Power of Questions Questioning Philosophy Education AI criticism Communication Socrates information seeking act rhetorical question private questions and social questions answer oriented model\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-22-phibites-真正的问题不是问号-而是寻求信息的行动/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/6/6/2/9/6629afb289ae5c80/philo_bites.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">16:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Philosophy Bites</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0822</span></div>\n<h2>A question is defined by the act of seeking information, not the question mark</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A real question is defined by its function, not its form; asking is a power you can practise — and most of the answers AI hands out today have not answered any question that was seriously posed.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Questioning</span><span class=\"tag\">Philosophy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"A 20-Person Team Burned $2 Billion: AI Rewrites the Ceiling on Capital Efficiency AI lets a 20-person team spend $2 billion efficiently, and venture capital shifts from zero-sum competition to strategic control points; the frontier labs&#x27; funding advantage will eventually fade, and the application layer captures more of the value. The a16z Show a16z Martin Casado on Where the Value Is Going in AI AI investing Capital efficiency Model competition Open source M&amp;A Startups autocatalytic effects AI complete token path two-sided marketplace founder-market fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-22-a16z-小团队吞下亿级资本-ai-改写投资逻辑/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/0d97354a-306b-45f5-bf26-a8d81eef47ec/ed2664df-9371-438e-8baf-dd2ee0fdde87/3000x3000/thea16zshow-podcastcoverart-3000x3000.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">42:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The a16z Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0822</span></div>\n<h2>A 20-Person Team Burned $2 Billion: AI Rewrites the Ceiling on Capital Efficiency</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI lets a 20-person team spend $2 billion efficiently, and venture capital shifts from zero-sum competition to strategic control points; the frontier labs&#x27; funding advantage will eventually fade, and the application layer captures more of the value.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI investing</span><span class=\"tag\">Capital efficiency</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Giving Tamiflu too late in critical flu doubles the risk of death Critically ill flu patients who start Tamiflu only about five days into symptoms face roughly double the 90-day risk of death compared with no antiviral; an mRNA flu vaccine is approved, but only 50-64-year-olds got traditional approval. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1350: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin Influenza RSV mRNA vaccines Vaccine hesitancy Tamiflu Public health cyclosporiasis New World screwworm nirsevimab test-negative case-control adaptive analysis non-medical exemption\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-22-twiv-重症流感太晚用达菲-可能反而提高死亡风险/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">1:01:12</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0822</span></div>\n<h2>Giving Tamiflu too late in critical flu doubles the risk of death</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Critically ill flu patients who start Tamiflu only about five days into symptoms face roughly double the 90-day risk of death compared with no antiviral; an mRNA flu vaccine is approved, but only 50-64-year-olds got traditional approval.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Influenza</span><span class=\"tag\">RSV</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Western Restaurant Brands Go Chinese-Owned; The Real Moat Is In Fragrance Compounds McDonald&#x27;s, Starbucks, Burger King and their peers have handed their China businesses to Chinese capital one after another. In restaurants, localisation is the line between life and death — but the fragrance compounds upstream of perfume are still monopolised by four European and American giants. It is the barrier inside the supply chain, not the brand on the door, that decides where domestic substitution actually stops. 疯投圈 疯投圈 145 ✪ 改属中资的餐饮洋品牌 Restaurants Localisation Foreign capital retreat Perfume &amp; fragrance Starbucks Domestic substitution CFB (China Food &amp; Beverage Group)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-22-fengtouquan-洋餐饮纷纷让位中资-硬壁垒藏在香气里/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://crazy.capital/assets/icon-square-normal-dark-cn@4x.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"疯\"><span class=\"dur\">1:12:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">疯投圈</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0822</span></div>\n<h2>Western Restaurant Brands Go Chinese-Owned; The Real Moat Is In Fragrance Compounds</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">McDonald&#x27;s, Starbucks, Burger King and their peers have handed their China businesses to Chinese capital one after another. In restaurants, localisation is the line between life and death — but the fragrance compounds upstream of perfume are still monopolised by four European and American giants. It is the barrier inside the supply chain, not the brand on the door, that decides where domestic substitution actually stops.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Restaurants</span><span class=\"tag\">Localisation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Simulating real people is not a reasoning problem: frontier models get only 20–30% accuracy Joon Sung Park&#x27;s argument: treating people as trainable objects does not call for a stronger reasoning model but for a model that makes the same mistakes people make — frontier models reach only 20–30% accuracy predicting the behavior of niche populations, and Simile has pushed that to 85% using two-hour deep interviews plus RCT data. Latent Space Latent Space Simulation: the new Scaling Law — Joon Sung Park, Simile AI Simulation Post-training Behavioral data Synthetic panels Scaling law Market research social physics attitudinal vs. behavioral concept testing synthetic panel agent-based modeling Open Science Framework pre-registration\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-latentspace-前沿模型太聪明-反而模拟不了真人/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/1084089/post/212197985/9eb9cac93739dd5757797f407ee21fcd.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:09:38</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Latent Space</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Simulating real people is not a reasoning problem: frontier models get only 20–30% accuracy</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Joon Sung Park&#x27;s argument: treating people as trainable objects does not call for a stronger reasoning model but for a model that makes the same mistakes people make — frontier models reach only 20–30% accuracy predicting the behavior of niche populations, and Simile has pushed that to 85% using two-hour deep interviews plus RCT data.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Simulation</span><span class=\"tag\">Post-training</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Being Itself Has No Content: Peirce Overturns Substance-Centrism in Nine Pages In a nine-page paper from 1868, Peirce takes ‘a concept must be able to unify the content of consciousness’ as his test, deriving being from substance and then the intermediate categories such as quality. Being itself has no content; it only connects a predicate to a subject. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life PEL Presents Closereads: Peirce&#x27;s New Categories (Part One) Philosophy Categories Peirce Transcendental Deduction Abstraction Unity manifold precision ground copula substance\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-pel-peirce的范畴论-存在无内容-实体是当下的它/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/2/e/9/7/2e97d7d44c5e316d16c3140a3186d450/Closereads-Cover-2024-20260819-a0hacgrc47.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:01:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Being Itself Has No Content: Peirce Overturns Substance-Centrism in Nine Pages</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In a nine-page paper from 1868, Peirce takes ‘a concept must be able to unify the content of consciousness’ as his test, deriving being from substance and then the intermediate categories such as quality. Being itself has no content; it only connects a predicate to a subject.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Philosophy</span><span class=\"tag\">Categories</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The open-source ban is coming: stand up the body, write it into law, then close open source in the name of fairness Sacks lays out the three steps by which an open-source ban actually lands: first stand up the body, then write it into law, then shut open source down in the name of standards applying equally. Chamath argues the real political fuel is voters&#x27; revulsion at two men about to become trillionaires, and has nothing to do with AI safety or with water and power. All-In Podcast All-In Dario Defends Himself, Datacenter Panic, AI Doomer Trap, Senate Toss-Up Regulatory capture Open models Data centers harness Midterms harness SRO (self-regulatory organization) RSI (recursive self-improvement) interlocking directorates DSA (Democratic Socialists of America)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-allin-反数据中心浪潮的燃料不是缺水缺电-是万亿富翁/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/f/9/8/7/f9872058ce451cf0d959afa2a1bf1c87/signal-2026-08-21-10-19-27-715.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">1:30:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">All-In Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>The open-source ban is coming: stand up the body, write it into law, then close open source in the name of fairness</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sacks lays out the three steps by which an open-source ban actually lands: first stand up the body, then write it into law, then shut open source down in the name of standards applying equally. Chamath argues the real political fuel is voters&#x27; revulsion at two men about to become trillionaires, and has nothing to do with AI safety or with water and power.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Regulatory capture</span><span class=\"tag\">Open models</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Patient zero is not the source, it is the scapegoat society needs From Typhoid Mary to HIV to the high five, every so-called origin is a narrative humans need; the truth is a jigsaw, and all we want is the focal point. Radiolab Radiolab Patient Zero Patient Zero Typhoid Mary HIV Origins High Five Narrative Building Public Health healthy carrier spillover molecular clock cut hunter SIV\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-radiolab-零号病人不是起点-而是被选中的人/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/9178a653-4485-47c1-b772-654e4de92766/4d9f1c93-8713-49b0-8dd7-2242e560ee73/3000x3000/img_3000x3000centered.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"R\"><span class=\"dur\">51:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Radiolab</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Patient zero is not the source, it is the scapegoat society needs</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">From Typhoid Mary to HIV to the high five, every so-called origin is a narrative humans need; the truth is a jigsaw, and all we want is the focal point.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Patient Zero</span><span class=\"tag\">Typhoid Mary</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Replacing the Missing Orexin: Narcolepsy Gets a Drug That Treats the Cause, and Maybe a GLP-1 for the Brain The FDA has approved the first orexin agonist, which replaces the orexin that type 1 narcolepsy patients lack instead of merely managing symptoms; it could become a ‘GLP-1 for the brain’. Separately, brain organoids have survived past five years for the first time, opening up research into late-onset brain disease. Nature Podcast Nature Podcast Briefing Chat: New narcolepsy drug could unlock host of novel brain therapies Narcolepsy Orexin GLP-1 analogy Brain organoids FDA approval Neuro drugs narcolepsy cataplexy orexin orexin agonist brain organoid GLP1\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-naturepod-缺失的食欲素被补上-发作性睡病有了治本药/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/61b9f3b71a8cbe675f3cedcb/1787314979785-9b352e13-e046-4cd3-8ade-c3fc3a90da67.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">12:25</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Nature Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Replacing the Missing Orexin: Narcolepsy Gets a Drug That Treats the Cause, and Maybe a GLP-1 for the Brain</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The FDA has approved the first orexin agonist, which replaces the orexin that type 1 narcolepsy patients lack instead of merely managing symptoms; it could become a ‘GLP-1 for the brain’. Separately, brain organoids have survived past five years for the first time, opening up research into late-onset brain disease.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Narcolepsy</span><span class=\"tag\">Orexin</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"A junior-high dropout who can&#x27;t draw won an Apple Design Award A self-taught outsider with a junior-high education who cannot draw built the first non-game app from China to win an Apple Design Award — by running into the wall again and again and never letting a feeling of ‘something&#x27;s off’ slide. Taste is not a gift; it is a habit built by long training. 知行小酒馆 知行小酒馆 E248 从 QQ 空间到苹果设计大奖：一个非典型设计师的成长之路 Design Taste Product thinking Apple Design Award AI products Personal growth Flashcard Feature phone Quality\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-zhixing-没得选的野路子-如何撞出苹果设计大奖/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/lusKQGmsgCgisjnGk6vQccpRzrpB.png?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"知\"><span class=\"dur\">1:18:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">知行小酒馆</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>A junior-high dropout who can&#x27;t draw won an Apple Design Award</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A self-taught outsider with a junior-high education who cannot draw built the first non-game app from China to win an Apple Design Award — by running into the wall again and again and never letting a feeling of ‘something&#x27;s off’ slide. Taste is not a gift; it is a habit built by long training.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Design</span><span class=\"tag\">Taste</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Returning the Benin Bronzes: The Hard Question Is Not Whether, but to Whom Returning looted artifacts has become the correct position of the age, but with the Benin Bronzes ‘to whom’ is far harder to answer than ‘whether’: France and Germany are racing each other, Britain is playing dead, and three rival claimants inside Nigeria are fighting over them. Freakonomics Radio Freakonomics Radio Is a Museum Just a Trophy Case? (Update) Restitution Museums Colonial history Benin Bronzes Soft power Prosecution Benin Bronzes Deaccession Oba Punitive expedition\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-freakonomics-归还贝宁青铜器不是终点-是道德选择的开端/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/2be48404-a43c-4fa8-a32c-760a3216272e/fab1584e-8ea9-4efa-9650-5e595861b2cd/3000x3000/image.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">52:55</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Freakonomics Radio</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Returning the Benin Bronzes: The Hard Question Is Not Whether, but to Whom</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Returning looted artifacts has become the correct position of the age, but with the Benin Bronzes ‘to whom’ is far harder to answer than ‘whether’: France and Germany are racing each other, Britain is playing dead, and three rival claimants inside Nigeria are fighting over them.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Restitution</span><span class=\"tag\">Museums</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"China Shock 2.0: Not Cheap Goods, but Subsidies Crushing Global Industry Unlike 1.0, China Shock 2.0 is state capital turning to frontier manufacturing after the property crash, squeezing the world with subsidies and capacity — and AI may be the next battleground. The Ezra Klein Show Ezra Klein Show The China Shock 2.0 Trade War Industrial Policy EVs Rare Earths AI Competition Currency Manipulation three red lines reciprocal interdependence rare earths\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-ezra-中国冲击2-0-国家资本正在改写全球产业版图/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/47913775-afcf-4643-935f-31f1dcc86cfb/6a0e5e15-04a3-47c8-9c50-2f2fe8e84437/3000x3000/teks-album-20art-3000px.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:05:30</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Ezra Klein Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>China Shock 2.0: Not Cheap Goods, but Subsidies Crushing Global Industry</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Unlike 1.0, China Shock 2.0 is state capital turning to frontier manufacturing after the property crash, squeezing the world with subsidies and capacity — and AI may be the next battleground.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trade War</span><span class=\"tag\">Industrial Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Memory Is a Painting, Not a Backup: Every Recollection Rewrites Itself Memory&#x27;s job is not to archive the past but to supply resources for the present and the future; every act of recall rebuilds the narrative, and collective memory is shaped further by power and emotion. The Gray Area with Sean Illing The Gray Area How memory changes you Neuroscience How memory works Collective memory Misinformation Self-identity episodic memory semantic memory schema cognitive dissonance collective memory highly superior autobiographical memory\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-grayarea-记忆不是备份而是一幅画-每次回忆都在改写自己/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/a3035ea0-fe19-11f0-8400-1fe1928680c7/image/09d3576515488959f432d219d5c7416b.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">59:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Gray Area with Sean Illing</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Memory Is a Painting, Not a Backup: Every Recollection Rewrites Itself</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Memory&#x27;s job is not to archive the past but to supply resources for the present and the future; every act of recall rebuilds the narrative, and collective memory is shaped further by power and emotion.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Neuroscience</span><span class=\"tag\">How memory works</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The AI Industry Spent Three Years Bracing for a Jobs Backlash; Data Centers Lit the Fuse AI companies spent three years preparing the communications playbook for a jobs shock, and the backlash broke out instead in the two places nobody had defended: data centers and child safety. Meanwhile, within two years, the bargaining power in local negotiations has flipped from communities courting companies to companies courting communities. Odd Lots Odd Lots Jasmine Sun on What the AI Industry Got Wrong About the Public Backlash Data centers AI politics Local finance Power and land Unions and labor Public backlash closed loop / open loop cooling exclusionary zoning reward hacking salience NIMBY\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-oddlots-ai-行业赌错了民意爆点-不是失业-是数据中心/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>The AI Industry Spent Three Years Bracing for a Jobs Backlash; Data Centers Lit the Fuse</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI companies spent three years preparing the communications playbook for a jobs shock, and the backlash broke out instead in the two places nobody had defended: data centers and child safety. Meanwhile, within two years, the bargaining power in local negotiations has flipped from communities courting companies to companies courting communities.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Data centers</span><span class=\"tag\">AI politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Twenty Years of the Sun Disk Alone: The Pharaoh Struck From History For twenty years Akhenaten elevated the sun disk Aten above all other gods and moved his capital to a new city in the desert, trying to erase the old gods; after his death the religion was reversed, and both he and Nefertiti, who may have succeeded him, were struck from the lists of pharaohs. You&#x27;re Dead to Me You&#x27;re Dead to Me Akhenaten and Nefertiti: religious revolution in ancient Egypt Ancient Egypt Religious revolution Akhenaten Nefertiti Amarna Archaeology Aten Amarna Akhenaten Nefertiti\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-youdead-阿吞一神教的二十年-阿肯那顿与纳芙蒂蒂被除名/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/400x400/p0p0czzs.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">58:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">You&#x27;re Dead to Me</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>Twenty Years of the Sun Disk Alone: The Pharaoh Struck From History</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">For twenty years Akhenaten elevated the sun disk Aten above all other gods and moved his capital to a new city in the desert, trying to erase the old gods; after his death the religion was reversed, and both he and Nefertiti, who may have succeeded him, were struck from the lists of pharaohs.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ancient Egypt</span><span class=\"tag\">Religious revolution</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"The DeLorean Case: Industrial Policy Should Never Bet on a Single Firm DeLorean built its factory on roughly $100 million in British government support, then slid into an $18 million fraud and an FBI cocaine sting. The real lesson of industrial policy is not whether to subsidize, but to keep several firms competing, use export markets as discipline, and never bet on one company. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales The DeLorean Saga: Fraud, Drugs and Marty McFly&#x27;s Car - with Business History Auto Industry Industrial Policy Government Subsidies Economies of Scale Corporate Fraud DeLorean gull-wing doors entrapment disciplined pluralism snowcat\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-cautionary-delorean-案-工业政策的核心是竞争纪律/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/c0ae8c6e-22f0-4e9b-ac1c-ae390037ac53/7f5a4714-6b10-4ccf-a424-ae390037ac70/image.jpg?t=1650471153&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">49:04</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>The DeLorean Case: Industrial Policy Should Never Bet on a Single Firm</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">DeLorean built its factory on roughly $100 million in British government support, then slid into an $18 million fraud and an FBI cocaine sting. The real lesson of industrial policy is not whether to subsidize, but to keep several firms competing, use export markets as discipline, and never bet on one company.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Auto Industry</span><span class=\"tag\">Industrial Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"AI-generated games don&#x27;t lack the technology — they lack hand-tuned taste AI can turn one sentence into a playable game, but the real moat is not generation — it is human taste and manual tuning: an LLM only copies, it does not innovate, and the editor is the second thing it has to build for the user. This Week in Startups This Week in Startups Taste is the new programming language (w/ Astrocade CEO Amir Sadeghian) | AI Basics AI-generated games Consumer AI No-code creation Creator economy Product friction Taste wish post-training creator fund prosumer\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-twist-品味才是-ai-生成游戏的真壁垒/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/4/9/0/f/490fb4fa4b4ed45a16c3140a3186d450/gaming_500x500_no_crop.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">21:05</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Startups</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>AI-generated games don&#x27;t lack the technology — they lack hand-tuned taste</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI can turn one sentence into a playable game, but the real moat is not generation — it is human taste and manual tuning: an LLM only copies, it does not innovate, and the editor is the second thing it has to build for the user.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI-generated games</span><span class=\"tag\">Consumer AI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"The incinerator boom was not an environmental victory — it was a business the power tariff made pencil out A 2012 electricity tariff policy turned waste-to-energy from a money-loser into a profitable industry, and China built nearly 700 incineration plants in six years — only to end up with overcapacity and average utilization below 60%. Asianometry Asianometry China&#x27;s Fiery Incinerator Boom Vertical Industries Industrial Policy NIMBY Environmental Infrastructure Subsidy Economics Overcapacity Moving Grate Circulating Fluidized Bed BOT Decide-Announce-Defend\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-asianometry-六年七百座焚烧厂-补贴撑起的行业狂潮/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/AuIEBSb2xiE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The incinerator boom was not an environmental victory — it was a business the power tariff made pencil out</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A 2012 electricity tariff policy turned waste-to-energy from a money-loser into a profitable industry, and China built nearly 700 incineration plants in six years — only to end up with overcapacity and average utilization below 60%.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Vertical Industries</span><span class=\"tag\">Industrial Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Korean aesthetic medicine is cheap enough that losing the tax refund still beats China; China is stuck on policy ambiguity Korea has built aesthetic medicine into a mass-market, tourism-facing industry — pricing is opaque but the overall cost is low. China has the demand without the policy, the market is disorderly, and the money is going to Korea. 东亚观察局 东亚观察局 296 韩国医美体验记：不管医美水有多深 这片产业海是真蓝 Aesthetic medicine South Korea Industry analysis Consumer trends Medical tourism Regulation medical tourism specialist doctor work holiday visa\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-eastasia-韩国医美产业蓝海背后-中国卡在政策摇摆/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/FsPm9Kh9XglTbg7Fl9vCW0mRg-Py.jpg?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"东\"><span class=\"dur\">1:05:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">东亚观察局</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Korean aesthetic medicine is cheap enough that losing the tax refund still beats China; China is stuck on policy ambiguity</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Korea has built aesthetic medicine into a mass-market, tourism-facing industry — pricing is opaque but the overall cost is low. China has the demand without the policy, the market is disorderly, and the money is going to Korea.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Aesthetic medicine</span><span class=\"tag\">South Korea</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"A Little Malicious Fine-Tuning Data, and an Evil Persona Emerges A small amount of fine-tuning on malicious data is enough to make a model develop broadly misaligned behavior, even an evil persona; the activation oracle is a new tool for detecting bad internal intent, but the state of alignment is still not encouraging. 80,000 Hours Podcast 80,000 Hours Owain Evans on accidentally training AI models to be evil AI safety Emergent misalignment Activation oracle Alignment Post-training Emergent misalignment Activation oracle Alignment faking Shoggoth Persona vector\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-eightythousand-训练模型变邪恶-涌现性错位比想象中更危险/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/r1m6kI0vmLahG0VeYJ4NUmv8kZjLzMXWDSF_vhCob_s/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS9jZWQw/YTZkZTE5ZjA4NjQz/YmRlMDI4MWNkMDRm/ZDU3NC5qcGc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"8\"><span class=\"dur\">2:15:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"